    "durationMs": 190973,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully tested. Implementation summary:\n\n**Stack**: ASP.NET Core 8 minimal API + EF Core 8 with Npgsql (idiomatic relational persistence), PostgreSQL via `DATABASE_URL` (parsed to an Npgsql connection string, nothing hard-coded).\n\n**Endpoints** (all verified with curl):\n- `POST /links` → 201 `{\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\":0}` with the URL echoed unchanged; random 8-char code when omitted; duplicate custom code → 409; malformed JSON / missing or non-http(s) URL / no host / invalid code (outside `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`) → 422 with an `error` field. Uniqueness is enforced by a unique index and races are retried.\n- `GET /links/{code}` → 200 with `{\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\"}`, unknown → 404.\n- `GET /r/{code}` → 302 with `Location` = stored URL, one atomic `clicks + 1` update per request, unknown → 404.\n- `GET /links` → 200 `{\"items\":[...],\"total\":n}` in ascending creation order.\n\n**Persistence**: EF migration `InitialCreate` (unique index on `Code`) applied at startup before serving, so `sh start.sh` applies pending migrations then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`. I verified data and click counts survive a restart, and a cold start recreates the database from scratch.\n\n**Files**: `Program.cs`, `Link.cs`, `AppDbContext.cs`, `DatabaseConfig.cs`, `Migrations/`, executable `start.sh`, README with a \"Starting the server\" section, plus a dotnet-tools manifest with dotnet-ef 8.0.11. I left the server stopped and the database dropped so the test run begins pristine — `sh start.sh` will create and migrate everything on boot."
  }
